# One mutant per line: the guard it removes (Mut("NAME") in the model), the
# setup check.sh runs it in, and the rule that must break. The rule must
# hold in that setup without the mutant, so each line shows that the guard
# keeps it. NAME+NAME removes each guard it names: for a guard that another
# one backs, it shows that the guard keeps the rule once the other is gone.
#
# MUTANT                       SETUP             RULE
# RemoveFlow.tla
PlanWithYes                    remove/no-faults  OnlyListedWorktreesMove
ConfirmSendsChoice             remove/no-faults  ConfirmSendsTheList
ConfirmSendsChoice             remove/no-faults  OnlyListedWorktreesMove
ChosenUnfiltered               remove/no-faults  OpensOnlyForCanGo
ChecksButtonForEveryVerdict    remove/no-faults  OpensOnlyForCanGo
NotModal                       remove/no-faults  ListIsForYourChoice
RunErrorSaysNothingMoved       remove/no-faults  NothingMovedIsTrue
ConfirmTwice+ConfirmWhileBusy  remove/no-faults  OneRemovalAtATime
CloseWhileBusy+ConfirmWhileBusy remove/no-faults  OneRemovalAtATime
NoRunGuard                     remove/draw       OneRemovalAtATime
NoRunGuard                     remove/reload     OneRemovalAtATime
NoMarker                       remove/reload     OneRemovalAtATime
ConfirmWhileBusy               remove/draw       OneRemovalAtATime
ConfirmWhileBusy               remove/reload     OneRemovalAtATime
# SaveFlow.tla. --expect (NoExpect) backs install's own read: residue
# compares again right before it writes, so the guards of that read keep
# their rules only once NoExpect is gone too.
NoExpect                       save/during       SaveIsWhatTheDialogShowed
NoExpect                       save/during       ReplacesOnlyWhatItShowed
NoExpect                       save/during       NeverDropsAnArgument
NoBasisCheck+NoExpect          save/outside      ReplacesOnlyWhatItShowed
NoBasisCheck+NoExpect          save/outside      SaveIsWhatTheDialogShowed
BasisWithoutMode+NoExpect      save/outside      ReplacesOnlyWhatItShowed
BasisWithoutVersion+NoExpect   save/outside      SaveIsWhatTheDialogShowed
RetryOnChange                  save/outside      ReplacesOnlyWhatItShowed
SendsTheScreenBasis            save/outside      ReplacesOnlyWhatItShowed
NoBlockedCheck+NoBasisCheck+NoExpect save/outside NeverDropsAnArgument
SwitchInstalls                 save/outside      WarnedBeforeItDeletes
ChoicesWhileBusy               save/outside      PreviewIsOfTheTickedFolders
ChoicesWhileBusy               save/outside      SaveIsOfTheTickedFolders
LeaveWhileSaving               save/outside      TheDialogStaysWhileItSaves
NoChangeGuard                  save/reload       OneChangeAtATime
NoChangeGuard+NoExpect         save/reload       ReplacesOnlyWhatItShowed
# save/copy: a save with the app's own copy. The copy check and --expect
# each keep the residue a save installs to the one the dialog showed, so
# either guard holds the rule alone.
NoPutBack                      save/copy         FailedSaveKeepsTheResidue
CachedVersion+NoCopyCheck      save/copy         SaveIsWhatTheDialogShowed
NoCopyCheck+NoExpect           save/copy         SaveIsWhatTheDialogShowed
